      "source": "rem 47-smooth Triangular Numbers\nrem https://projecteuler.net/problem=581\nuse numbers\nuse sequences\nuse io\nuse cli\narg B integer = 10000000000000\nLimit = 2 * B + 1\n\nrem Add one prime's allowable powers.\nfun Values extend Prime\n  Bound = Limit // Prime\n  Front = Values\n  for Front len greater 0\n    Front = Front (Front at most Bound)\n    Front = Front * Prime\n    Values = concat Values Front\n  end\n  return Values\nend\nPrimes = primes till 48 copy\nSeed = array 1\nSmooth = Primes reduce extend with Seed\nSmooth = Smooth sort\nrem Neighbouring smooth integers give\nrem every smooth triangular index.\nNext' = Smooth shift -1\nGood = Next - Smooth equal 1\nAnswer = Smooth Good sum\nAnswer print\n"
    },
